    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "SOUTHWEST\nJULY 6, 2004 FLIGHT SCHEDULE\nAs a Senior Attorney,\nI'm happy to provide\nlegal assistance to\nour departments.",
      "Pacific\nSeattle/Tacoma\nSpokane\nPortland\nBoise\nSacramento\nOakland\n(San Francisco Area) •\nSan Jose\n(San Francisco Area\n• Reno/Tahoe\nSalt Lake City\nLas Vegas\nBurbank\nOntario\nLos Angeles\n• (Palm Springs Area)\n(LAX) Orange County\nSan Diego\nTUCSON\nMountain\nCentrai\ncastern\nA DUQUeTCUt\n(Santa Fe Area\nEl Paso\nAmarillo\nLubbock\nMidland/\nOdessa\nOmaha\nKansas City\nTulsa •\nOklahoma City\n(Love Field)\nAustin\nBuffalo/\nNiagara Falls\nChicago\nCleveland\nColumbus\nIndianapolis\nSt. Louis ®\n* Louisville\nNashville\nLittle Rock\nBirmingham\nJackson\nSan Antonio\nCorpus\nHouston\n(Hobby \u0026\nintercontinental)\nNew orleans\nTampa\nBay\n• Harlingen/South Padre Island\nManchester\nboston Areal\nAlbany •\n• Providence (Boston Area)\nHartford/Springfield\n~ Long Island/Islip\nPhiladelphia\nBaltimore/\nWashington (BWI)\n(D.C. Area)\nNorfolk\n(Southern Virginia)\nRaleigh-Durham (RDU)\nJacksonville\norando\nWest Palm Beach\nFt. Lauderdale\n(Miami Area)\nNew nonstop service starts July 6, 2004.\nNew nonstop service starts August 8, 2004.\nIndianapolis, Phoenix, and Tucson do not observe daylight-saving time.\nVisit us at southwest.com® for an up-to-date\nflight schedule.\nYou can now check in for your flight and print\nyour boarding pass at southwest.com or at\nthe Southwest Skycap,* Ticket Counter,\nRAPID CHECK-IN Kiosk, or at your gate at\nleast one hour prior to departure. (20 minutes\nprior to scheduled departure, boarding pass\ndistribution is available at the Departure\nGate only.)\nCargo Customers, mail requests to:\nCargo Customer Schedule List, HDQ/3CM,\nP.O. Box 36611, Dallas, TX 75235-1611.\nAll other correspondence should be sent to:\nSouthwest Airlines Co.,\nP.O. Box 36611, Dallas, TX 75235-1611.\n*Where available\nSOUTHWEST\n2005.\n132.047"
    ],
